    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 11.28,
      "end": 17.33,
      "text": "Not necessarily. Many old pianos come back nicely, though it might need a few tunings to settle."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 20.02,
      "end": 27.23,
      "text": "After so long, the strings have dropped way below pitch. Pulling them up all at once is risky, so tuners often do it in stages."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 30.57,
      "end": 34.37,
      "text": "I'm fairly sure about it, but I could be wrong. What sounds off to you?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 36.69,
      "end": 43.54,
      "text": "A single tuning isn't too bad, but if it needs repairs as well, it adds up. A tuner can tell you on the first visit if it's worth it."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 51.04,
      "end": 55.99,
      "text": "Then it's worth a look. Even if it's not perfect, it carries a lot of memories, and that matters too."
